xnu 0152: the touch wiring is measured; read the id and the reports

0151 found the QUP4 lane order by reading the product id: the four pads carry
cs gpio19, clk gpio18, mosi gpio17 and miso gpio16, not the order the device
tree implies. With that order the 0xAA boot-option echo comes back and
0x00010014 answers the version block (42 45 52 4c 49 4e at the start of the
data, rom_vid 02 00 04, patch_pid "9916R"), which is exactly what the working
driver's brl_read_version prints.

Fix the wiring, verify the echo, print the id and the IC info block at 0x10070
(touch_data_addr 0x00010308, 8-byte head, 8-byte points, both at the offsets
the packed struct gives), then start a kernel thread that polls IRQ (GPIO21,
active low), reads a report, hands every finger to MondrianHIDTouch through
neo5se_hid_touch(), and writes one zero byte back to the report address to
release the line. Polling at one tick first; GIC 305 and a real interrupt come
later.

--- a/bsd/dev/neo5se_touch.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/neo5se_touch.c
@@ -20,8 +20,11 @@
